From 943cbe35777c98ed6696f3c411acb3bd40a8e67e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agent Export <codex@agent.example>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 06:55:07 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] server: write prompt-cache disk spills on a background thread
 (--cache-disk-async)

A RAM eviction wrote its ~2 GiB entry to the disk tier on the server loop. On a
busy HDD that took 17-65 s per write, during which no request or /metrics was
served.

The disk tier's write() is split into plan_write (index work), write_file (file
I/O, no index access) and commit_write (index work); write() runs the three in
order, unchanged for existing callers. The prompt cache hands evicted entries
(moved, not copied) to one writer thread. disk_mtx guards the index; the
writer holds it only for plan and commit, never during the file I/O, so
lookups, restores and /metrics go on while a file is written.

--cache-disk-async N (LLAMA_ARG_CACHE_DISK_ASYNC, default 1) bounds entries
queued or being written; with the queue full an eviction is dropped and
counted instead of blocking. 0 = synchronous, as before. Shutdown/sleep
flushes drain the queue first. New metrics:
prompt_cache_disk_async_{pending,writes_total,drops_total,dropped_bytes_total}.

Tests: test-prompt-cache-disk 423/423 (10 repeated runs), and 3/3 under
ThreadSanitizer with no reports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
